Every file that carries copied or adapted text from the upstream project states its origin in a comment of this form, at the file header or at the ported section:

```
// Derived from Templater 2.26.0 (AGPL-3.0-only) src/<path>, with Inkstone adaptations.
```

The statement is in English because this repository holds every source comment to English (`scripts/check-i18n.mjs`); reader-facing Chinese lives in the locale catalogs, and a licence notice is not reader-facing copy.

Files that only follow the upstream *documented behaviour* without copying its text carry the opposite statement instead, so a reader can always tell derivation from independent implementation. This table lists the components, not the individual files; the per-file statements are authoritative.

The upstream licenses above also cover anything redistributed with Inkstone that came from those projects, so removing a derived file does not remove the obligation for a build that already shipped it.
